    <GaugingStation location="Briantspuddle" name="Piddle" number="44014">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Flat V crump weir for low flow monitoring.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Station bypassed substantially at high flows. Non-modular flow at about 0.55m. Well-maintained structure. Drowning is an issue due to weed growth but weed regularly cut. Bypassing and unstable bed. Some raising of banks upstream carried out in 2001 to reduce bypassing. One peak flow rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat V Crump weir 6.0m broad for low flow monitoring.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">No major flow regime influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly Lower Chalk with small outcrops of Middle and Upper Chalk forming higher ground flanking the catchment. Mainly pastoral with some arable agriculture on flatter ground. No major catchment changes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Rating under review using recent gaugings." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
